# Generate the focused Kotlin probe for the redundant-assertion shape.
# Run from the worktree root:
#   haxe tests/haxe/kotlin-redundant-assertion/kotlin-gen.hxml
# The emitted Kotlin is the measurement: after the first printed `!!` on an
# immutable nullable local, a second read of the same local inside the same
# expression must not print a second assertion.
# (RedundantAssertionCoverage)
#
# `-cp packages/compiler` is explicit on purpose: `-lib boring` resolves the
# nearest ancestor `.haxelib` projection, which in this workspace points at an
# older compiler (Class<PolicyQueries> has no field
# matchStructTypedefByUnification). Every hxml that generates here spells the
# source root out instead.
-lib reflaxe
-cp packages/compiler
-cp packages/compiler/reflaxe/kotlin/std-shadow
-cp packages/compiler/reflaxe/kotlin
-cp tests/haxe/kotlin-redundant-assertion/probe
-cp samples
--macro Intercept.run(['samples', 'tests/haxe/kotlin-redundant-assertion/probe'])
--macro kotlincompiler.Compiler.use()
-D kotlin-output=out/kotlin-redundant-assertion/gen
-D runtime-import=boring.runtime
-D runtime-emit=runtime
redundantassertion.RedundantAssertionOps
redundantassertion.MemberRegistryProbe
